{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0a85c7b1-9e7a-4614-b231-e3448a322436","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20bd374f0eca93a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-lhjak06o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view in the Dashboard (side-by-side and diff)\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the run comparison capability in the Dashboard: users can select two or more training and pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side, and switch to a diff view that highlights which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs. Today parameters and metrics live only on per-run pages, forcing comparison via exported spreadsheets; this epic makes comparison a first-class platform workflow that model promotion decisions can rely on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of two or more runs from the runs list in the Dashboard.\n- Side-by-side view of parameters and metrics for the selected runs.\n- Diff mode for two selected runs that highlights which parameters and metrics changed between them (the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface, delivered together with the side-by-side view).\n- The comparison works for both training runs and Data Science Pipelines runs. Data Science Pipelines is a passive component here — its run metadata is consumed as-is through existing interfaces, with no code change to Data Science Pipelines.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given two or more runs selected from the Dashboard runs list, when the user opens the comparison, then the parameters and metrics of all selected runs are displayed side by side.\n- Given two runs selected for comparison, when the user switches to the diff view, then the parameters and metrics that differ between the two runs are highlighted.\n- Given a selection that includes pipeline runs and training runs, then parameters and metrics render for both run types in the comparison.\n- The comparison for pipeline runs requires no code change to Data Science Pipelines components (passive-component validation).\n- No regression to existing per-run parameter and metric pages.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the run diff view highlighting which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1 — it is not separately schedulable and ships in this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36984,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96f48064cc04221b","agent_id":"a597df87e2ee14187","session_id":"f928a5ef-5578-4e6b-b331-0c0e02acb1a2","uuid":"2a062f98-a711-4ab2-9029-8e7e370ba6a1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:58:32.676Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015 into epics"}
