{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-994c4ef79b2e72d6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view in the Dashboard (side-by-side and diff) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Run lineage link-back on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n20\t\n21\t## Dependency DAG\n22\t\n23\t```mermaid\n24\tgraph TD\n25\t    E001[\"E001 Run comparison view (P0)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Open comparison from registry (P1)\"]\n26\t    E002[\"E002 Run lineage link-back (P1)\"] --> E003\n27\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Documentation (P1)\"]\n28\t    E002 --> E004\n29\t    E003 --> E004\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\t## DAG Justification\n33\t\n34\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n35\t|------|------|-----------|\n36\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different components, teams, and repos (odh-dashboard vs model-registry); no shared artifacts — the lineage link-back does not need the comparison view to exist and vice versa. |\n37\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 | The registry entry point builds against the comparison view surface: it opens the comparison for the run that produced a model version. The consuming implementation is serial after the surface it targets. |\n38\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 | The registry UI entry point builds 