onent here — its run metadata is consumed as-is through existing interfaces, with no code change to Data Science Pipelines.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given two or more runs selected from the Dashboard runs list, when the user opens the comparison, then the parameters and metrics of all selected runs are displayed side by side.\n45\t- Given two runs selected for comparison, when the user switches to the diff view, then the parameters and metrics that differ between the two runs are highlighted.\n46\t- Given a selection that includes pipeline runs and training runs, then parameters and metrics render for both run types in the comparison.\n47\t- The comparison for pipeline runs requires no code change to Data Science Pipelines components (passive-component validation).\n48\t- No regression to existing per-run parameter and metric pages.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n53\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the run diff view highlighting which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1 — it is not separately schedulable and ships in this epic.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc6bf13b75b0bda6","agent_id":"ad860cbea3ed76465","session_id":"f928a5ef-5578-4e6b-b331-0c0e02acb1a2","uuid":"c828f35f-a883-48e4-9d58-28ebeec066e4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:00:44.873Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-818a2532fbd64d2c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
