\t- Given a model version registered from a pipeline run, the lineage reference works the same as for training runs.\n44\t- Given existing model versions that have no run reference, then they remain valid and retrievable (backward compatible; no migration required to keep the registry functional).\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry. This epic delivers the registry-side lineage; the registry-UI entry point that opens the comparison is delivered by the Dashboard-side epic for HLR-2.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc6bf13b75b0bda6","agent_id":"ad860cbea3ed76465","session_id":"f928a5ef-5578-4e6b-b331-0c0e02acb1a2","uuid":"a2a1f60f-d8bd-46cb-9b84-ba2e12f2e30c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:00:45.606Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad0308e9c68906d6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
