n for documentation work. Verify with the strategy author.\n55\t- **Passive component — Data Science Pipelines**: listed as affected but no HLR requires code changes to it; it is the source of pipeline-run parameters/metrics consumed by the Dashboard. Handled as a passive component: validation is an acceptance criterion on E001 (comparison renders parameters and metrics for pipeline runs as well as training runs, with no Data Science Pipelines code change). Risk, not an investigation: the strategy has no open questions, and both components are GA with documented interfaces (pipeline runs are already surfaced in the Dashboard per architecture context).\n56\t- **Docs epic priority above its HLR label**: E004 is P1 while HLR-4 is P2. This is the mandated `docs-authoring` priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1), not a priority inversion.\n57\t- **No priority inversions or scope traps** detected in the implementation epics.\n58\t\n59\t## Tiered Delivery\n60\t\n61\tNone — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is inside platform components that are GA and Konflux-onboarded.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c935442b5698a2","agent_id":"a5469e71909ee6a92","session_id":"f928a5ef-5578-4e6b-b331-0c0e02acb1a2","uuid":"51259d7e-378a-46d9-9a77-67dae3f5f16a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:03:59.212Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84b80dbbd6f90c7a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
