{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a97e028b96b344","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Run lineage link-back on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run lineage link-back on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes registered model versions link back to the run that produced them. The Model Registry becomes the source of truth for training lineage: every model version registered from a training or pipeline run carries a reference to that run, exposed through the Model Registry REST API so any consumer — including the Dashboard's registry UI — can resolve which run produced a given version and open a comparison from it.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Capture the reference to the producing run (training run or pipeline run) on registered model versions at registration time, using the documented extension point for structured metadata on model versions (custom properties).\n38\t- Expose the run reference through the Model Registry REST API so it is retrievable on model version views by platform consumers.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- Given a model version registered from a run, then the version carries a reference to the producing run that is retrievable via the Model Registry REST API.\n43\t- Given a model version registered from a pipeline run, the lineage reference works the same as for training runs.\n44\t- Given existing model versions that have no run reference, then they remain valid and retrievable (backward compatible; no migration required to keep the registry functional).\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry. This epic delivers the registry-side lineage; the registry-UI entry point that opens the comparison is delivered by the Dashboard-side epic for HLR-2.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c935442b5698a2","agent_id":"a5469e71909ee6a92","session_id":"f928a5ef-5578-4e6b-b331-0c0e02acb1a2","uuid":"25eeb2dd-f929-4931-b361-4e7522a6edd8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:03:59.874Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a97e028b96b344","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
